WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.200
With the release of 2021's Eternals, the Marvel&nbsp;
superhero known as Ajak will finally be coming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:09.520
to the silver screen, as portrayed by&nbsp;
Salma Hayek. But who exactly is Ajak,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:14.080
and why is the character so important to the&nbsp;
Eternals? This is Ajak's story explained.

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:17.680
Although they haven't always been at&nbsp;
the forefront of most fans' minds,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:21.200
the Eternals cast a huge shadow over&nbsp;
the history of the Marvel universe.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:25.840
Those mutations that make the X-Men so&nbsp;
uncanny? They're tied to the Eternals' origin.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:29.760
Thanos? He's involved with them too,&nbsp;
in a roundabout way: The Eternals&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:34.480
once colonized a little place called Titan,&nbsp;
which became home to Thanos centuries later.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:37.040
"I am… inevitable."

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:41.680
The Eternals are essentially the product of&nbsp;
experimentation, performed by an ancient,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:46.000
omnipotent group of super-sized humanoids&nbsp;
called the Celestials. The Celestials&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:50.560
tinkered with humanity's genetic code,&nbsp;
creating two offshoot races: The grotesque&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:55.600
creatures known as the Deviants, and the immortal,&nbsp;
super-powered beings that make up the Eternals.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.600 --> 00:01:00.080
Despite looking like humans, the Eternals&nbsp;
are very nearly divine in their abilities:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:04.080
They can control the aging process,&nbsp;
cast illusions, fly, read minds,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:08.400
and transform matter. Essentially, they are&nbsp;
gods, and have often ended up becoming the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:13.680
source of many of humanity's legends, religions,&nbsp;
and fables. For example, the Eternal Sersi was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:19.200
immortalized as Circe in Homer's Odyssey, while&nbsp;
Ikaris' life inspired the ancient tale of Icarus.

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:25.120
Like his fellow Eternals, Ajak has a rich&nbsp;
backstory of his own. However, to fully understand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:30.000
who he is, it's important to understand what he&nbsp;
can do. Ajak is equipped with superhuman strength,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.640
for one. He can also fly at speed, teleport,&nbsp;
and do almost everything that falls under the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:39.520
general category of "energy manipulation." When&nbsp;
it comes time to throw down against the bad guys,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:44.240
he's capable of projecting beams of heat and&nbsp;
concussive energy from his eyes and hands.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:48.720
He is also a brilliant archaeologist — perhaps&nbsp;
helped by the fact that he was around for much&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:53.280
of the history he digs up. In some of the latest&nbsp;
Eternals stories, Ajak has also been shown to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:58.160
have the power to change gender, although it's&nbsp;
uncertain how much of this constitutes a retcon.

00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:02.960
Uniquely, Ajak possesses an uncanny&nbsp;
ability to communicate with the Celestials.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:06.640
This is pretty much his signature ability&nbsp;
when it comes to protecting humanity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:10.800
as few other Eternals are able to do it.&nbsp;
And given that the Celestials have a habit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:13.920
of showing up every now and again to see&nbsp;
if they feel like destroying the Earth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:17.280
it's fair to say that Ajak's powers&nbsp;
are pretty vital to the team.

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:23.600
Ajak was born in the Eternal city of Polaria,&nbsp;
located in the Ural Mountains, to parents named&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:28.640
Rakar and Amaa. His branch of the species is&nbsp;
sometimes referred to as the Polar Eternals.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:32.400
Not much is known about Ajak prior to&nbsp;
the Celestials' intervention in his life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:37.600
but it is known that Ajak and his brother Arex&nbsp;
were active in ancient Greece around 1200 BC,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:42.320
where the former was either mistaken for&nbsp;
the mythical hero of the Trojan War, Ajax.

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:46.320
Unfortunately, there's very little information&nbsp;
about what happened to Arex after the brothers'&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:50.640
time in Greece came to an end. He pops&nbsp;
up only very rarely in the Marvel canon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:53.840
and the jury is out as to whether&nbsp;
or not he's even still alive.

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:59.120
After Greece, Ajak wandered the Earth,&nbsp;
making his way to places such as Babylon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:01.760
where he took on the Deviant leader, Warlord Kro.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:07.040
After that, he spent some time in the Americas,&nbsp;
where he was worshiped as a god. The Aztecs paid&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:11.440
tribute to him as Quetzalcoatl, one of the&nbsp;
wisest and most powerful of their deities.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:16.000
In time, the Incas also came to worship&nbsp;
Ajak as Tecumotzin, the Lord of Flight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:20.720
and Ajak wasn't shy about using his supreme&nbsp;
power to advance the civilizations he favored.

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:25.920
By 1000 AD, Ajak was an accomplished warrior,&nbsp;
cosmic genius, and influential figure in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:29.920
progress of humanity. While that would be enough&nbsp;
for most superheroes to hang their hats on,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:33.840
however, Ajak's greatest feats yet would&nbsp;
come with the return of the Celestials.

00:03:34.960 --> 00:03:39.680
Unable to escape his own past, Ajak crossed&nbsp;
paths with both the Celestials and the Deviants&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:43.520
once again, when the former returned to&nbsp;
Earth on a fact-finding mission. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.520 --> 00:03:47.680
is because Earth wasn't the only planet&nbsp;
the Celestials decided to experiment on:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:52.480
The home worlds of races such as the Skrulls and&nbsp;
the Kree got the same treatment, for example.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:55.840
To help judge whether or not they&nbsp;
had been a success, the Celestials&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.840 --> 00:04:00.320
subjected each race to four tests, or&nbsp;
"hosts," to deem them worthy of life.

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:05.200
During the Third Host, Ajak was living in Peru.&nbsp;
He acted as a liaison between the Celestials&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:09.840
and humanity, as well as a go-between for the&nbsp;
Celestials and the gods humanity had given rise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:14.800
to, such as Zeus of the Greek pantheon. Luckily,&nbsp;
humanity passed the test with flying colors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:18.640
and Ajak decided to put his atoms into&nbsp;
storage until the Celestials returned.

00:04:19.520 --> 00:04:22.480
Eventually, the Fourth Host of&nbsp;
Celestials returned to Earth to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.480 --> 00:04:27.040
see how their experiments were faring — kicking&nbsp;
off Ajak's story in the modern Marvel universe.

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:31.760
Ajak is awoken by Ikaris in&nbsp;
1976's Eternals #2. Soon after,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:35.600
the Celestials once again come to South&nbsp;
America, and settle on an Incan plateau&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:39.600
that Ajak has set up for them. And&nbsp;
once again, he acts as their liaison.

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:43.280
This time, however, their presence sparks&nbsp;
intervention from the likes of S.H.I.E.L.D.,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:45.600
as well as Odin and the forces of Asgard.

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:52.240
"Because that's -"

00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:53.760
"Because that's what heroes do."

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:57.600
Despite the combined efforts of all three&nbsp;
factions, Earth ends up losing the fight&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.600 --> 00:05:02.560
against the Celestials. However, the battle helps&nbsp;
the Celestials realize that humanity is worthy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.560 --> 00:05:05.200
and therefore, they agree to&nbsp;
let the Earth off the hook.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:08.400
Most of the important players have their&nbsp;
memories erased of the whole incident,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:12.480
and the Eternals realize they needn't worry&nbsp;
about the Celestials' interventions anymore.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.480 --> 00:05:16.320
So it's good news all around, but it&nbsp;
also means that Ajak is out of a job.

00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:22.320
During the Fourth Host event, Ajak befriends&nbsp;
a human archaeologist named Dr. Daniel Damian.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:25.360
After Ikaris brings the brilliant&nbsp;
doctor along to awaken Ajak,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:30.080
the two become thick as thieves — Damien even&nbsp;
watches the Fourth Host event take place from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:34.320
within the Celestials' impenetrable dome.&nbsp;
However, he is more interested in preserving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:37.840
the history of the Incas than he is in&nbsp;
making sure humanity passes its test.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:42.480
Damian begins with all the makings of&nbsp;
a classic superhero ally… but grief&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:47.040
does horrible things to people. His daughter,&nbsp;
Margo, flees the Celestials' city with Ikaris,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:51.440
while Damian agrees to stay behind to protect&nbsp;
history. Ikaris and Margo are separated,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.440 --> 00:05:55.680
and she is later turned into a Deviant&nbsp;
and killed in an attempt to get to Ikaris.

00:05:55.680 --> 00:06:00.720
In the wake of this tragedy, Damian seeks revenge&nbsp;
on Celestials, Deviants, Eternals — the lot of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.720 --> 00:06:05.040
them. Part of his plan includes an elaborate&nbsp;
trick against the Eternals and Deviants:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:09.120
specifically, he turns Ajak into a&nbsp;
literal monster. Needless to say,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:14.080
Damian's relationship with the Eternals sours, and&nbsp;
his friendship with Ajak dies a miserable death.

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:20.080
Damian's plan involves planting false prophecies&nbsp;
about the twin offspring of Eternals and Deviants&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:25.120
being the ones to eventually conquer both races.&nbsp;
He then uses advanced Celestial technology to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.120 --> 00:06:29.680
transform Ajak into a monster whose sole purpose&nbsp;
seems to be systematically hunting down and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:34.480
killing twin siblings on Earth. Thus mutated,&nbsp;
Ajak assists in the kidnapping of twins Donald&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.480 --> 00:06:39.200
and Deborah Ritter, the offspring of the Eternal&nbsp;
Thena and the Deviant Kro. Fortunately, the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:43.440
doctor's plan to kill the twins in front of their&nbsp;
parents fails when Ikaris gets wise to the whole&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:47.840
situation and, disgusted with his own actions,&nbsp;
Ajak disintegrates both himself and Damian.

00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:52.640
Luckily, this all happens in the world of comic&nbsp;
books, where death is merely a distraction.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:57.200
Ajak is eventually resurrected in the chambers&nbsp;
of the Eternal city of Olympia by an Eternal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.200 --> 00:07:01.680
named Sprite. Sprite is later revealed to be&nbsp;
deceiving Ajak and the other Eternals into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.680 --> 00:07:05.840
helping him use the power of the fabled&nbsp;
Dreaming Celestial to overwrite reality.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:10.720
Sprite's plot is thwarted, but it leads to an&nbsp;
enduring rivalry between Ajak and another Eternal;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.720 --> 00:07:13.360
one that would result in his&nbsp;
second death and resurrection.

00:07:14.240 --> 00:07:18.800
When the Dreaming Celestial is awoken, it&nbsp;
chooses the Eternal Makkari as its spokesperson.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.800 --> 00:07:21.680
Obviously, Ajak's experience&nbsp;
in this field is extensive,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.680 --> 00:07:26.320
so he understandably feels a little slighted&nbsp;
by this choice, and soon grows to hate Makkari.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.320 --> 00:07:30.960
He even hatches a plan to kill him — but&nbsp;
while Makkari does die, it doesn't stick.

00:07:30.960 --> 00:07:34.880
Now at loose ends, Ajak decides to travel the&nbsp;
world and learn as much as he can about the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.880 --> 00:07:39.200
Celestials. He lives in San Francisco for&nbsp;
a time, and even becomes a gardener. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.200 --> 00:07:43.760
journey eventually leads Ajak to join Hercules&nbsp;
in a battle with the Skrull Gods, in which he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.760 --> 00:07:48.880
squares off with a divine Skrull named Kly'bn.&nbsp;
It's during this fight that Ajak dies again.

00:07:48.880 --> 00:07:53.600
Again, this being the Marvel universe, Ajak's&nbsp;
death doesn't last. He returns to Earth and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.600 --> 00:07:58.080
travels to Olympia, where he lives among his&nbsp;
fellow Eternals. However, all this changes the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.080 --> 00:08:03.200
day dead Celestials rain from the sky, signaling&nbsp;
the arrival of the Dark Celestials on Earth.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:07.680
That's when the Eternals learn a terrible&nbsp;
secret about themselves and their existence;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.680 --> 00:08:11.520
one that leads all of them to either&nbsp;
turn on each other or kill themselves.

00:08:11.520 --> 00:08:15.040
Of course, once again, they've&nbsp;
all been revived. Ajak stars,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.040 --> 00:08:19.520
as a woman, alongside Makkari in the&nbsp;
2021 Eternals: Celestia one-shot.

